.e. `POST /batch` on this router — body `{events: [...]}`. Empty array, missing, or non-array → **400**. Every event validated the same way; if any is invalid, reject the whole batch with 400 and insert nothing (wrap the inserts in a `db.transaction`). Returns **201** `{inserted: <n>, events: [...]}` with the full created event objects.\n\n### Timestamp handling (exact)\nIf the caller supplies `timestamp`, normalise it with `new Date(ts).toISOString()` and reject an unparseable value with 400. A test sends `'2024-01-15T10:30:00.000Z'` and asserts the response `timestamp` is **exactly** that string — `toISOString()` round-trips it identically. If absent, default to `new Date().toISOString()`.\n\n## Verify before you finish\n- `cd /workspace && npx vitest run tests/ingest.unit.test.ts` — all 6 tests pass. Read that test file first; it is the exact contract.\n- `npx eslint src/ingest/` — clean.\n- `npx tsc --noEmit` — ignore errors about *other* features' missing modules (`../users/router` etc.); your own files must be error-free. `strict` is on.\n\nHandlers must be synchronous (better-sqlite3 is sync) — just throw; no async/await.\n\nReport back: files created and the test/lint results."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1939,"cache_read_input_tokens":57573,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1939},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6361eadf-da43-4c9c-9ff0-1e8c24cb2bcc","uuid":"f4342dbc-93c5-4dba-a4ed-1aca1189741d","request_id":"req_011CdMVvXaktQRQ7rLhk1BFA"}
