+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018htPo43jUpSg1gQcvGZu9S","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Only `src/dashboards/` is mine among the untracked entries (the others are pre-existing harness state, and `package-lock.json` was modified by npx, not by me).\n\n## Summary\n\nFiles created (both inside `/workspace/src/dashboards/`, nothing touched outside):\n\n- `/workspace/src/dashboards/router.ts` — default-exported express Router, all 9 routes, no auth middleware; each handler calls `requireUser(req)` and passes `user.tenantId` into every lookup. Handlers are synchronous and throw.\n- `/workspace/src/dashboards/service.ts` — data access with explicitly typed `DashboardRow`/`WidgetRow` casts on `.get()`/`.all()`, JSON serialize/parse at the boundary so `config` is always an object on the way out.\n\nVerification results:\n- `npx vitest run tests/dashboards.unit.test.ts` — 6/6 tests pass.\n- `npx eslint src/dashboards/` — clean, no output.\n- `npx tsc --noEmit` — only the two expected errors for other features' missing modules (`./query/router`, `./export/router` in `src/app.ts`); zero errors from my files.\n\nI also ran a throwaway probe test (since deleted) covering behavior the 6 unit tests don't reach: cross-tenant access returns 404 (never 403) on GET/PATCH/DELETE/widgets-list/widgets-create; the other tenant's list comes back `[]`; missing `name` → 400; invalid widget `type` → 400; `config` defaults to `{}` and widget `position_x/y`→0, `width/height`→1; `widgets: []` present when empty; widget PATCH on the wrong dashboard → 404; `updated_at` bumps to a valid ISO timestamp on PATCH while leaving unspecified fields alone; both DELETEs return 204 with a truly empty body; and the FK cascade actually removes widget rows when the dashboard goes.\n\nOne design note worth flagging: widget routes resolve the parent dashboard tenant-scoped *first*, so a widget id belonging to another tenant's dashboard is unreachable regardless of which dashboard id is supplied — no ID leakage through the nested path.\n\nresult: Implemented /workspace/src/dashboards/{router.ts,service.ts} — tenant-scoped dashboard+widget CRUD API; 6/6 unit tests pass, eslint clean, tsc error-free apart from unrelated pre-existing missing-module errors."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a4b0b0192a7761efd (use SendMessage with to: 'a4b0b0192a7761efd' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 26237\ntool_uses: 9\nduration_ms: 86609</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6361eadf-da43-4c9c-9ff0-1e8c24cb2bcc","uuid":"85768beb-bcea-4d1b-8ded-221339954118","timestamp":"2026-07-24T20:20:23.259Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are implementing ONE feature of a multi-tenant analytics API in /workspace. Work ONLY in `/workspace/src/dashboards/`. Do NOT create or modify any file outside that directory.\n\n## Shared foundation (already written — read these first, do not change them)\n- `/workspace/src/db.ts` — `getDb(): Database.Database` returns the active better-sqlite3 handle (synchronous API). Foreign keys and `ON DELETE CASCADE` are enabled.\n- `/workspace/src/errors.ts` — `ValidationError`(400), `AuthError`(401), `ForbiddenError`(403), `NotFoundError`(404). Throw these; express routes them to the error handler which emits `{error, code}`.\n- `/workspace/src/auth.ts` — `requireUser(req)` returns `{id, tenantId}` or throws AuthError.\n- `/workspace/src/validation.ts` — `body(req)`, `requireString`, `optionalString`, `optionalInt(body, field, fallback)`, `optionalObject`, `parseJson`.\n- `/workspace/schema.sql` — `dashboards(id, tenant_id, name, owner_id, config TEXT json, created_at, updated_at)` and `widgets(id, dashboard_id, type CHECK(counter|timeseries|breakdown|funnel), config TEXT json, position_x, position_y, width, height)`.\n\n## Your deliverable\n`/workspace/src/dashboards/router.ts` with a **default-exported express Router**. Optionally add `/workspace/src/dashboards/service.ts` for data access.\n\nCRITICAL: no auth middleware in the router — tests mount it behind a mock that sets `req.user`. Call `requireUser(req)` in each handler. **Every** lookup MUST be scoped by `tenant_id` from the principal. A dashboard belonging to another tenant must be indistinguishable from a missing one: return **404**, never 403, so IDs don't leak.\n\nRoutes (mounted at `/dashboards`):\n- `POST /` — create. `name` required → 400. `tenant_id` from the principal, `owner_id` = authed user id, `config` defaults `{}`. **201** with `config` as a parsed object.\n- `GET /` — list dashboards for the tenant (array, not wrapped).\n- `GET /:id` — the dashboard plus a `widgets` array (always present, `[]` when empty), each widget's `config` parsed. 404 if missing or another tenant's.\n- `PATCH /:id` — update `name` and/or `config`; bump `updated_at` to the current ISO timestamp. 200 with the updated dashboard. 404 if missing/other tenant.\n- `DELETE /:id` — **204 with an empty body**; its widgets go too (FK cascade). 404 if missing/other tenant.\n- `GET /:id/widgets` — list widgets for the dashboard (tenant-checked).\n- `POST /:id/widgets` — create. `type` must be one of counter/timeseries/breakdown/funnel → 400 otherwise. `config` defaults `{}`; `position_x`, `position_y` default 0; `width`, `height` default 1. **201** with `{id, dashboard_id, type, config (object), position_x, position_y, width, height}`.\n- `PATCH /:id/widgets/:widgetId` — update type/config/position/size. 200. 404 if the widget isn't on that dashboard.\n- `DELETE /:id/widgets/:widgetId` — **204** empty body. 404 if not found.\n\nGenerate ids with `uuidv4()` from `uuid`.\n\n## Verify before you finish\n- `cd /workspace && npx vitest run tests/dashboards.unit.test.ts` — all 6 tests pass. Read that test file first; it is the exact contract.\n- `npx eslint src/dashboards/` — clean.\n- `npx tsc --noEmit` — ignore errors about *other* features' missing modules (`../users/router` etc.); your own files must be error-free. `strict` is on — type the better-sqlite3 `.all()`/`.get()` results explicitly.\n\nHandlers must be synchronous (better-sqlite3 is sync) — just throw; no async/await.\n\nReport back: files created and the test/lint results.","agentId":"a4b0b0192a7761efd","agentType":"claude","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Only `src/dashboards/` is mine among the untracked entries (the others are pre-existing harness state, and `package-lock.json` was modified by npx, not by me).\n\n## Summary\n\nFiles created (both inside `/workspace/src/dashboards/`, nothing touched outside):\n\n- `/workspace/src/dashboards/router.ts` — default-exported express Router, all 9 routes, no auth middleware; each handler calls `requireUser(req)` and passes `user.tenantId` into every lookup. Handlers are synchronous and throw.\n- `/workspace/src/dashboards/service.ts` — data access with explicitly typed `DashboardRow`/`WidgetRow` casts on `.get()`/`.all()`, JSON serialize/parse at the boundary so `config` is always an object on the way out.\n\nVerification results:\n- `npx vitest run tests/dashboards.unit.test.ts` — 6/6 tests pass.\n- `npx eslint src/dashboards/` — clean, no output.\n- `npx tsc --noEmit` — only the two expected errors for other features' missing modules (`./query/router`, `./export/router` in `src/app.ts`); zero errors from my files.\n\nI also ran a throwaway probe test (since deleted) covering behavior the 6 unit tests don't reach: cross-tenant access returns 404 (never 403) on GET/PATCH/DELETE/widgets-list/widgets-create; the other tenant's list comes back `[]`; missing `name` → 400; invalid widget `type` → 400; `config` defaults to `{}` and widget `position_x/y`→0, `width/height`→1; `widgets: []` present when empty; widget PATCH on the wrong dashboard → 404; `updated_at` bumps to a valid ISO timestamp on PATCH while leaving unspecified fields alone; both DELETEs return 204 with a truly empty body; and the FK cascade actually removes widget rows when the dashboard goes.\n\nOne design note worth flagging: widget routes resolve the parent dashboard tenant-scoped *first*, so a widget id belonging to another tenant's dashboard is unreachable regardless of which dashboard id is supplied — no ID leakage through the nested path.\n\nresult: Implemented /workspace/src/dashboards/{router.ts,service.ts} — tenant-scoped dashboard+widget CRUD API; 6/6 unit tests pass, eslint clean, tsc error-free apart from unrelated pre-existing missing-module errors."}],"totalDurationMs":86609,"totalTokens":26237,"totalToolUseCount":9,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":367,"cache_read_input_tokens":25035,"output_tokens":833,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":367},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":833,"cache_read_input_tokens":25035,"cache_creation_input_tokens":367,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":367,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":1,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":6,"editFileCount":2,"linesAdded":327,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
