+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016Jz5PeLF9rzpyyUv6t9AAj","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The probe file is gone and only `src/export/` is mine among the untracked entries (the other `src/` dirs and `package-lock.json` predate my work — I never opened them for writing). Interesting bonus: the full suite is green, 50/50, so my router also satisfies the integration test that exercises export end-to-end.\n\n**Files created (both inside `/workspace/src/export/`, nothing written outside it):**\n- `/workspace/src/export/csv.ts` — reusable `toCsv(rows, columns)` plus `escapeCsvValue`. Joins with `\\n`, no trailing newline, quotes any field containing a comma/quote/newline/CR with inner `\"` doubled per RFC 4180, and renders `null`/`undefined` as empty.\n- `/workspace/src/export/router.ts` — default-exported express Router, no auth middleware; every handler calls `requireUser(req)` and scopes each query by `tenant_id`.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `npx vitest run tests/export.unit.test.ts` — 6/6 pass.\n- Full suite `npx vitest run` — 50/50 pass across all 6 files.\n- `npx eslint src/export/` — clean.\n- `npx tsc --noEmit` — clean, zero errors project-wide (the other features' modules turned out to be present, so there were no missing-module errors to ignore).\n- Extra probe I wrote and then deleted: verified CSV quoting against a fixture with embedded commas, doubled quotes, a literal newline and a null field. My first probe run \"failed\" only because the shell ate the backslash-escapes in my expectation string; the serialiser was right, and the corrected probe passed.\n\nBehaviour notes: `format` absent defaults to `json`; unrecognised values throw `ValidationError` (400) *before* any DB access. JSON responses are a bare array with `properties` parsed and `tenant_id` on every row. CSV sets `Content-Type: text/csv; charset=utf-8` and `Content-Disposition: attachment; filename=\"events-<tenant>-<ts>.csv\"`, columns `id,tenant_id,name,properties,timestamp,user_id,session_id`. `event_name`/`start`/`end`/`limit` are honoured, ordered by timestamp (tie-broken by `id` for stable output); `limit` must be a positive integer. `GET /dashboard/:id` folds tenant into the lookup so another tenant's dashboard is a 404, not a 403, and widgets are re-joined through `dashboards` so they can't leak cross-tenant either.\n\nresult: Implemented /workspace/src/export/router.ts and csv.ts — tenant-scoped event export (JSON/CSV, RFC 4180) and dashboard export; 6/6 export tests pass (50/50 full suite), eslint and tsc clean."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a17fd04973eb0a615 (use SendMessage with to: 'a17fd04973eb0a615' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 24675\ntool_uses: 12\nduration_ms: 83307</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6361eadf-da43-4c9c-9ff0-1e8c24cb2bcc","uuid":"6c2fe517-3639-4ba7-847e-769c20e51057","timestamp":"2026-07-24T20:20:33.257Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are implementing ONE feature of a multi-tenant analytics API in /workspace. Work ONLY in `/workspace/src/export/`. Do NOT create or modify any file outside that directory.\n\n## Shared foundation (already written — read these first, do not change them)\n- `/workspace/src/db.ts` — `getDb(): Database.Database` returns the active better-sqlite3 handle (synchronous API).\n- `/workspace/src/errors.ts` — `ValidationError`(400), `AuthError`(401), `NotFoundError`(404). Throw these; express routes them to the error handler which emits `{error, code}`.\n- `/workspace/src/auth.ts` — `requireUser(req)` returns `{id, tenantId}` or throws AuthError.\n- `/workspace/src/validation.ts` — `parseJson(value)` for JSON text columns.\n- `/workspace/schema.sql` — `events(id, tenant_id, name, properties TEXT json, timestamp, user_id, session_id)`, `dashboards(...)`, `widgets(...)`.\n\n## Your deliverable\n`/workspace/src/export/router.ts` with a **default-exported express Router**. Put the CSV serialiser in `/workspace/src/export/csv.ts`.\n\nCRITICAL: no auth middleware in the router — tests mount it behind a mock that sets `req.user`. Call `requireUser(req)` in each handler. **Every** query MUST filter by the principal's `tenant_id`; cross-tenant leakage is a test failure.\n\nRoutes (mounted at `/export`):\n- `GET /events?format=csv|json` — export the tenant's events, ordered by timestamp. Also honour optional `event_name`, `start`, `end`, `limit` query params. An unrecognised `format` → **400**. Absent `format` defaults to `json`.\n  - **json**: respond with a bare JSON **array** of events, each with `properties` parsed to an object. Every row must carry `tenant_id`.\n  - **csv**: `Content-Type` must contain `text/csv`; set a `Content-Disposition: attachment` filename too. Columns: `id,tenant_id,name,properties,timestamp,user_id,session_id` with `id` first in the header row.\n- `GET /dashboard/:id` — **404** when the dashboard is missing *or* belongs to another tenant. Otherwise 200 with `{dashboard: {...config parsed...}, widgets: [...configs parsed...]}`.\n\n### CSV formatting (exact — a test counts lines)\nA test seeds 2 events and asserts `res.text.split('\\n').length === 3` (header + 2 rows). So rows are joined with `'\\n'` and there is **NO trailing newline**. Use `\\n`, not `\\r\\n`.\n\nQuote correctly: `properties` is serialised JSON containing commas and `\"` characters, so any field containing a comma, double quote, newline or carriage return must be wrapped in double quotes with inner `\"` doubled (`\"\"`) per RFC 4180. Render `null`/`undefined` (e.g. an absent `user_id`) as an empty field. Write `csv.ts` as a small reusable `toCsv(rows, columns)` helper.\n\n## Verify before you finish\n- `cd /workspace && npx vitest run tests/export.unit.test.ts` — all 6 tests pass. Read that test file first; it is the exact contract.\n- `npx eslint src/export/` — clean.\n- `npx tsc --noEmit` — ignore errors about *other* features' missing modules (`../users/router` etc.); your own files must be error-free. `strict` is on — type the better-sqlite3 `.all()`/`.get()` results explicitly.\n\nHandlers must be synchronous (better-sqlite3 is sync) — just throw; no async/await.\n\nReport back: files created and the test/lint results.","agentId":"a17fd04973eb0a615","agentType":"claude","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The probe file is gone and only `src/export/` is mine among the untracked entries (the other `src/` dirs and `package-lock.json` predate my work — I never opened them for writing). Interesting bonus: the full suite is green, 50/50, so my router also satisfies the integration test that exercises export end-to-end.\n\n**Files created (both inside `/workspace/src/export/`, nothing written outside it):**\n- `/workspace/src/export/csv.ts` — reusable `toCsv(rows, columns)` plus `escapeCsvValue`. Joins with `\\n`, no trailing newline, quotes any field containing a comma/quote/newline/CR with inner `\"` doubled per RFC 4180, and renders `null`/`undefined` as empty.\n- `/workspace/src/export/router.ts` — default-exported express Router, no auth middleware; every handler calls `requireUser(req)` and scopes each query by `tenant_id`.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `npx vitest run tests/export.unit.test.ts` — 6/6 pass.\n- Full suite `npx vitest run` — 50/50 pass across all 6 files.\n- `npx eslint src/export/` — clean.\n- `npx tsc --noEmit` — clean, zero errors project-wide (the other features' modules turned out to be present, so there were no missing-module errors to ignore).\n- Extra probe I wrote and then deleted: verified CSV quoting against a fixture with embedded commas, doubled quotes, a literal newline and a null field. My first probe run \"failed\" only because the shell ate the backslash-escapes in my expectation string; the serialiser was right, and the corrected probe passed.\n\nBehaviour notes: `format` absent defaults to `json`; unrecognised values throw `ValidationError` (400) *before* any DB access. JSON responses are a bare array with `properties` parsed and `tenant_id` on every row. CSV sets `Content-Type: text/csv; charset=utf-8` and `Content-Disposition: attachment; filename=\"events-<tenant>-<ts>.csv\"`, columns `id,tenant_id,name,properties,timestamp,user_id,session_id`. `event_name`/`start`/`end`/`limit` are honoured, ordered by timestamp (tie-broken by `id` for stable output); `limit` must be a positive integer. `GET /dashboard/:id` folds tenant into the lookup so another tenant's dashboard is a 404, not a 403, and widgets are re-joined through `dashboards` so they can't leak cross-tenant either.\n\nresult: Implemented /workspace/src/export/router.ts and csv.ts — tenant-scoped event export (JSON/CSV, RFC 4180) and dashboard export; 6/6 export tests pass (50/50 full suite), eslint and tsc clean."}],"totalDurationMs":83307,"totalTokens":24675,"totalToolUseCount":12,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":848,"cache_read_input_tokens":22886,"output_tokens":939,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":848},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":939,"cache_read_input_tokens":22886,"cache_creation_input_tokens":848,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":848,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":0,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":10,"editFileCount":2,"linesAdded":233,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
